WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.740
Hindu scriptures picture the
divine filling everything:

2
00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:07.330
every atom, every person, every animal.

3
00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:11.210
Yet an ancient Upanishad
looks somewhere much smaller:

4
00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:14.880
a self the size of a thumb,
in the middle of the body.

5
00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:20.450
If God is everywhere, why do Hindus also
look for God inside their own heart?

6
00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:24.860
In this mission, you'll read verses from
the Upanishads and the Bhagavad Gita

7
00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:27.380
about where the divine can be found.

8
00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:32.650
Then you'll see why different Hindu traditions
rank these ideas in different orders.

9
00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:37.700
Your mission: find out why Hindus look
inside the heart for a God they believe

10
00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:38.920
is everywhere.
